  "lineage": "Kabyle music of the Tamazight-speaking Berber population of the Kabylie mountains of northern Algeria. Performance integrates classical Kabyle-language poetic-meter (the asefru four-line verse-form developed by seventeenth-century poet Si Mohand) with Berber pentatonic-leaning modal vocabulary distinct from Andalusi-Arab. The mid-twentieth-century Paris-emigration produced an exile-and-protest corpus through Slimane Azem; 1970s-1980s cultural-revival under Idir and Lounès Matoub. The 1998 Matoub assassination politicized the genre. Instrumentation: oud, mandole (Algerian electric-mandolin), bendir frame-drum.",
